# Two Chains of Mephistopheles: "the effect is cumulative ... each of them will modify each draw ... the player must discard
# if possible. Once the player fails to discard and instead 'mills' a card, all further effects of additional Chains of
# Mephistopheles will not do anything" (its ruling; CR 614.5). Bot1 holds the Forest and an Island as Ancestral Recall
# resolves in its turn 3 main phase:
# - the first draw: one Chains has Bot1 discard the Forest and draw, and the other replaces that draw - Bot1 discards the
#   Island and draws a card, which neither Chains replaces again;
# - the second: Bot1 discards that card for the first Chains and would draw, but for the second it has nothing to discard,
#   so it mills a card and draws nothing;
# - the third: nothing to discard for the first Chains, so a card is milled and nothing is drawn, and nothing is left for the
#   second to replace.
# Bot1 ends with an empty hand: three cards discarded, two milled, one drawn (and discarded).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Chains of Mephistopheles
Chains of Mephistopheles
Ancestral Recall
Forest
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Chains of Mephistopheles.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chains of Mephistopheles.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand = Mox Sapphire; Ancestral Recall; Forest; Island
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Choose(Forest)
Bot1.Choose(Island)
Bot1.Choose(Island)
! Bot1.Choose
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 16
Bot1.Graveyard = Ancestral Recall; Island; Island; Island; Island; Forest; Black Lotus
